{"type":"message","id":"f5d08f7f","parentId":"6cdab1f0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:14:50.097Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a specific change needed after upgrading to version 5.19. They mention that for each agent, you need to add:\n\n```json\n\"tools\": {\n  \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"]\n}\n```\n\nFrom the config-tools.md I read, I don't see any `tools.allowlist` field. There's `tools.allow` and `tools.deny`. Let me check if there's an `allowlist` field, or if this might be a new field in 5.19.\n\nLet me search the config schema for this.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-6876779d-a746-4183-a912-e06fe9558e60","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"allowlist\\|allow.*list\" | head -30"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | grep -i \\\"allowlist\\\\|allow.*list\\\" | head -30\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-62142183-773e-407f-8960-39cc47cd0a0c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d, indent=2))\" 2>/dev/null | grep -A5 -B5 \"allowlist\" | head -60"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d, indent=2))\\\" 2>/dev/null | grep -A5 -B5 \\\"allowlist\\\" | head -60\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":29715,"output":241,"cacheRead":320,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30276,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779340476519,"responseId":"chatcmpl-635ebda1-7e8c-488a-a9b8-dbcddce6dc86"}}
