{"type":"message","id":"80fcd181","parentId":"dc800930","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:17:14.050Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the context - the user is asking about v5.19 where each agent needs to add:\n```\n\"tools\": {\n \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"]\n}\n```\n\nThis seems like they're asking about a specific change in OpenClaw 5.19 where messaging tools need explicit allowlisting per agent. Let me check the agent-level tools config more carefully.\n\nFrom the config schema output I found earlier:\n- Per-agent tools config has `allowlist` (tool allowlist additions)\n- Per-agent also has `messageActionAllowlist` for message actions like \"send\"\n\nThe user's format `{\"tools\": {\"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"]}}` doesn't match the per-agent structure I found. \n\nLooking at what they're describing - allowing `message` and `channels` tools - this aligns with the messaging profile which includes `message` and related session tools. But the schema shows `allowlist` and `alsoAllow` are arrays for tool IDs, and there's a separate `messageActionAllowlist` for fine-grained message actions. The format they provided doesn't quite fit either pattern, so I need to reconsider what they're actually asking for.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ba9cf3a6-6248-4d85-88c9-23bebab7c4ef","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndef find_tools_structure(obj, path=''):\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n        if 'tools' in obj.get('properties', {}):\n            print(f'Found tools at {path}')\n            print(json.dumps(obj['properties']['tools'], indent=2)[:4000])\n            print('---')\n        for k,v in obj.items():\n            find_tools_structure(v, path+'.'+k if path else k)\n    elif isinstance(obj, list) and len(obj) > 0:\n        find_tools_structure(obj[0], path)\nfind_tools_structure(d)\n\" 2>/dev/null"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json,sys\\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\\ndef find_tools_structure(obj, path=''):\\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\\n        if 'tools' in obj.get('properties', {}):\\n            print(f'Found tools at {path}')\\n            print(json.dumps(obj['properties']['tools'], indent=2)[:4000])\\n            print('---')\\n        for k,v in obj.items():\\n            find_tools_structure(v, path+'.'+k if path else k)\\n    elif isinstance(obj, list) and len(obj) > 0:\\n        find_tools_structure(obj[0], path)\\nfind_tools_structure(d)\\n\\\" 2>/dev/null\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":32091,"output":410,"cacheRead":544,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33045,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779340616808,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a9c9d959-7a79-4b5b-bc29-9f2199855046"}}
{"type":"message","id":"4c66ec10","parentId":"80fcd181","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:17:22.969Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-ba9cf3a6-6248-4d85-88c9-23bebab7c4ef","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found tools at \n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"profile\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"const\": \"minimal\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"const\": \"coding\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"const\": \"messaging\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"const\": \"full\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Tool Profile\",\n      \"description\": \"Global tool profile name used to select a predefined tool policy baseline before applying allow/deny overrides. Use this for consistent environment posture across agents and keep profile names stable.\"\n    },\n    \"allow\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Tool Allowlist\",\n      \"description\": \"Absolute tool allowlist that replaces profile-derived defaults for strict environments. Use this only when you intentionally run a tightly curated subset of tool capabilities.\"\n    },\n    \"alsoAllow\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Tool Allowlist Additions\",\n      \"description\": \"Extra tool allowlist entries merged on top of the selected tool profile and default policy. Keep this list small and explicit so audits can quickly identify intentional policy exceptions.\"\n    },\n    \"deny\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Tool Denylist\",\n      \"description\": \"Global tool denylist that blocks listed tools even when profile or provider rules would allow them. Use deny rules