{"type":"message","id":"0458fde6","parentId":"521c5c81","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:17:58.472Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the schema. The user is asking about a `\"tools\": { \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"] }` pattern. But looking at the schema, there's no `allowlist` at the top level of `tools`. There's `allow`, `alsoAllow`, `deny`, etc.\n\nWait - let me re-read what the user said: \"升级到新版本5.19后需要为每个agent添加这个嘛：请添加一下 `\"tools\": { \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"] }`\"\n\nMaybe they mean something specific to their setup or a specific agent type? Let me check if there's something in the agent config that uses `allowlist`.\n\nActually looking at the schema output I see in `properties.agents.properties.list.items` there's a `tools` section with `allow`, `alsoAllow`, `deny` etc. But no `allowlist` directly.\n\nWait - could they be referring to the `message` tool's action allowlist? Looking at the schema:\n\nIn tools section:\n```\n\"message\": {\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    ...\n    \"allowlist\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"title\": \"Message Action Allowlist\",\n      \"description\": \"Global message action allowlist for the message tool. Use only when the whole runtime should expose and accept a reduced action set; prefer per-agent allowlists for public or sandboxed agents.\"\n```\n\nAh! So there's a `message` tool with an `allowlist` for actions!\n\nAnd for per-agent:\n```\n\"messageActionAllowlist\": {\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n  \"title\": \"Agent Message Action Allowlist\",\n  \"description\": \"Per-agent message action allowlist for the message tool. Set to a minimal list such as [\\\"send\\\"] for public sandbox agents so read, edit, delete, reaction, and other provider-specific message actions stay hidden and blocked.\"\n```\n\nSo the pattern `\"tools\": { \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"] }` might be user's shorthand for configuring something like the message tool's action allowlist, or maybe a misunderstanding of the actual schema structure.\n\nLet me look at the full message tool schema to understand what `allowlist` actually controls there.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-3762eaf8-b6ae-4bc1-a20f-cc885b2c2c92","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndef find_message_tool(obj, path=''):\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n        if 'message' in obj.get('properties', {}):\n            print(f'Found message at {path}')\n            print(json.dumps(obj['properties']['message'], indent=2)[:3000])\n        for k,v in obj.items():\n            find_message_tool(v, path+'.'+k if path else k)\n    elif isinstance(obj, list) and obj:\n        find_message_tool(obj[0], path)\nfind_message_tool(d)\n\" 2>/dev/null"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json,sys\\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\\ndef find_message_tool(obj, path=''):\\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\\n        if 'message' in obj.get('properties', {}):\\n            print(f'Found message at {path}')\\n            print(json.dumps(obj['properties']['message'], indent=2)[:3000])\\n        for k,v in obj.items():\\n            find_message_tool(v, path+'.'+k if path else k)\\n    elif isinstance(obj, list) and obj:\\n        find_message_tool(obj[0], path)\\nfind_message_tool(d)\\n\\\" 2>/dev/null\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":39063,"output":652,"cacheRead":320,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40035,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779340645077,"responseId":"chatcmpl-2b077d98-4e0f-4813-a8b4-f2db938e0821"}}
{"type":"message","id":"68c870f4","parentId":"0458fde6","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:18:07.574Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-3762eaf8-b6ae-4bc1-a20f-cc885b2c2c92","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found message at properties.agents.properties.list.items.properties.tools\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"allowCrossContextSend\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"crossContext\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allowWithinProvider\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Agent Cross-Context Messaging (Same Provider)\",\n          \"description\": \"Per-agent message guard for sending to other conversations on the same provider. Set false for current-conversation-only public agents.\"\n        },\n        \"allowAcrossProviders\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Agent Cross-Context Messaging (Across Providers)\",\n          \"description\": \"Per-agent message guard for sending across providers. Keep false for public or sandboxed agents.\"\n        },\n        \"marker\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"enabled\": {\n              \"type\": \"boolean\"\n            },\n            \"prefix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"suffix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allow\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Agent Message Action Allowlist\",\n          \"description\": \"Per-agent message action allowlist for the message tool. Set to a minimal list such as [\\\"send\\\"] for public sandbox agents so read, edit, delete, reaction, and other provider-specific message actions stay hidden and blocked.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"broadcast\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"enabled\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}\nFound message at properties.tools\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"allowCrossContextSend\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"title\": \"Allow Cross-Context Messaging\",\n      \"description\": \"Legacy override: allow cross-context sends across all providers.\"\n    },\n    \"crossContext\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allowWithinProvider\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Allow Cross-Context (Same Provider)\",\n          \"description\": \"Allow sends to other channels within the same provider (default: true).\"\n        },\n        \"allowAcrossProviders\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Allow Cross-Context (Across Providers)\",\n          \"description\": \"Allow sends across different providers (default: false).\"\n        },\n        \"marker\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"enabled\": {\n              \"type\": \"boolean\",\n              \"title\": \"Cross-Context Marker\",\n              \"description\": \"Add a visible origin marker when sending cross-context (default: true).\"\n            },\n            \"prefix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"title\": \"Cross-Context Marker Prefix\",\n              \"description\": \"Text prefix for cross-context markers (supports \\\"{channel}\\\").\"\n            },\n            \"suffix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"title\": \"Cross-Context Marker Suffix\",\n              \"description\": \"Text suffix for cross-context markers (supports \\\"{channel}\\\").\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allow\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Message Action Allowlist\",\n          \"description\": \"Global message action allowlist for the message tool. Use only when the whole runtime should expose and accept a reduced action set; prefer per-agent allowlists for public or sandboxed agents.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"broadcast\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"enabled\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Enable Message Broadcast\",\n          \"description\": \"Enable broadcast action (default: true).\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":9033,"aggregated":"Found message at properties.agents.properties.list.items.properties.tools\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"allowCrossContextSend\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"crossContext\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allowWithinProvider\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Agent Cross-Context Messaging (Same Provider)\",\n          \"description\": \"Per-agent message guard for sending to other conversations on the same provider. Set false for current-conversation-only public agents.\"\n        },\n        \"allowAcrossProviders\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Agent Cross-Context Messaging (Across Providers)\",\n          \"description\": \"Per-agent message guard for sending across providers. Keep false for public or sandboxed agents.\"\n        },\n        \"marker\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"enabled\": {\n              \"type\": \"boolean\"\n            },\n            \"prefix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"suffix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allow\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Agent Message Action Allowlist\",\n          \"description\": \"Per-agent message action allowlist for the message tool. Set to a minimal list such as [\\\"send\\\"] for public sandbox agents so read, edit, delete, reaction, and other provider-specific message actions stay hidden and blocked.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"broadcast\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"enabled\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}\nFound message at properties.tools\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"allowCrossContextSend\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"title\": \"Allow Cross-Context Messaging\",\n      \"description\": \"Legacy override: allow cross-context sends across all providers.\"\n    },\n    \"crossContext\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allowWithinProvider\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Allow Cross-Context (Same Provider)\",\n          \"description\": \"Allow sends to other channels within the same provider (default: true).\"\n        },\n        \"allowAcrossProviders\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Allow Cross-Context (Across Providers)\",\n          \"description\": \"Allow sends across different providers (default: false).\"\n        },\n        \"marker\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"enabled\": {\n              \"type\": \"boolean\",\n              \"title\": \"Cross-Context Marker\",\n              \"description\": \"Add a visible origin marker when sending cross-context (default: true).\"\n            },\n            \"prefix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"title\": \"Cross-Context Marker Prefix\",\n              \"description\": \"Text prefix for cross-context markers (supports \\\"{channel}\\\").\"\n            },\n            \"suffix\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"title\": \"Cross-Context Marker Suffix\",\n              \"description\": \"Text suffix for cross-context markers (supports \\\"{channel}\\\").\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"allow\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Message Action Allowlist\",\n          \"description\": \"Global message action allowlist for the message tool. Use only when the whole runtime should expose and accept a reduced action set; prefer per-agent allowlists for public or sandboxed agents.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"broadcast\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"enabled\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"title\": \"Enable Message Broadcast\",\n          \"description\": \"Enable broadcast action (default: true).\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779340687571}}
{"type":"message","id":"35e33249","parentId":"68c870f4","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:19:01.808Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have a complete picture. Let me analyze the user's question:\n\nThe user says after upgrading to 5.19, they need to add for each agent:\n```json\n\"tools\": {\n  \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"]\n}\n```\n\nBut looking at the schema, there is NO `allowlist` field under `tools` at the agent level. The schema shows:\n- `tools.allow` - Tool Allowlist (replaces profile-derived defaults)\n- `tools.alsoAllow` - Tool Allowlist Additions (additive)\n- `tools.deny` - Tool Denylist\n\nThe user's example uses `allowlist` which doesn't exist. They might be confused with:\n1. `tools.actions.allow` - which is for message actions (like \"send\", \"read\", etc.)\n2. The per-agent `tools` structure has `actions.allow` for message action allowlisting\n\nOr they might be thinking of a different structure entirely. Let me re-read their question. They said:\n\"请添加一下\" (please add this) - `\"tools\": { \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"] }`\n\nThis is confusing because `message` and `channels` are not tool names - they're more like groups or action categories. Looking at the schema more carefully:\n\n- `group:messaging` is a tool group that contains `message`\n- There is no `channels` tool or group\n\nActually wait - maybe they're talking about something else entirely. Let me think about what \"channels\" could be... In some contexts, \"channels\" might refer to the messaging channels concept.\n\nBut actually I think the user might have received some guidance or documentation that mentioned adding something specific, and they're asking me if this is correct. Since I don't have context about where this recommendation came from, I should:\n\n1. Clarify that the schema doesn't have an `allowlist` field directly under `tools`\n2. Show what the actual structure looks like\n3. Ask for clarification on what they're trying to achieve\n\n\n4. The schema simply doesn't support a direct `allowlist` field within `tools` at the agent level, so either this is a misunderstanding or referring to something else entirely\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n根据我对 OpenClaw 5.19 配置 schema 的检查，**每个 agent 添加 `tools.allowlist` 这种写法在当前版本不是有效配置**。\n\n让我解释一下实际情况：\n\n## 5.19 的 Agent Tools 配置结构\n\n每个 agent 的 `tools` 配置支持以下字段（来自 schema）：\n\n```json5\n{\n  // Agent 级别 tools 配置\n  \"profile\": \"coding\",           // minimal | coding | messaging | full\n  \"allow\": [\"message\"],           // 绝对允许列表（替换 profile 默认）\n  \"alsoAllow\": [\"message\"],       // 在 profile 基础上额外允许\n  \"deny\": [],                    // 禁用列表\n  \"actions\": {                   // message 工具的操作白名单\n    \"allow\": [\"send\"]             // 如 [\"send\"] 表示只允许发消息\n  },\n  \"crossContext\": { ... }         // 跨会话发消息控制\n}\n```\n\n## 关键点\n\n1. **没有 `allowlist` 字段** — 正确字段名是 `allow`（绝对允许）或 `alsoAllow`（附加允许）\n2. **`message` 是工具名**，`channels` 不是有效的工具或组名\n3. **如果你想让 agent 使用 `message` 工具**，正确写法是：\n   ```json5\n   {\n     \"agents\": {\n       \"list\": [{\n         \"id\": \"your-agent\",\n         \"tools\": {\n           \"alsoAllow\": [\"message\"]\n         }\n       }]\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n## 你遇到的情况\n\n你提到需要为每个 agent 添加：\n```json\n\"tools\": {\n  \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"]\n}\n```\n\n这个 `allowlist` 写法**不是 5.19 的有效配置**。可能来源：\n- 旧版本的写法（如果有的话）\n- 第三方文档或 AI 生成的错误建议\n- 或者你记错了具体内容？\n\n**你能否确认这个配置是来自哪里（文档/升级指南/AI建议）？** 这样我可以帮你判断是否需要替代方案，或者这是一个需要报告的问题。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":40413,"output":884,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41393,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779340687578,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9ab9b0c0-0ba4-469a-9340-52e36df175cf"}}
